{"uid":"ee45a1b8b0a6d1e2","name":"test_only_the_first_of_several_consecutive_external_only_claims_is_corroborated_the_rest_back_off_instead_of_stagnating","fullName":"tests.test_progress_pin_task015#test_only_the_first_of_several_consecutive_external_only_claims_is_corroborated_the_rest_back_off_instead_of_stagnating","historyId":"e9becc25d3a072632c9181ed22aa145a","time":{"start":1791942135858,"stop":1791942135961,"duration":103},"description":"Four consecutive `external`-only claims on one task, no other\n    witness: the first is honoured at face value (corroborated); the\n    second is requirement A.5's letter 3 own case (\"two consecutive\n    external-only claims\" -- the second does not get the grace the first\n    did, so it is an ordinary stagnation witness, old counter -> 1).\n\n    PRD v0.29 #279 cure (task 014's sweep): the THIRD and FOURTH no longer\n    reach the old three-strike guard at all -- the second and third\n    consecutive uncorroborated claims are ALSO the first two of #279's own\n    re-poll streak, so the third claim is #279's own `consecutiveCount: 2`\n    trigger (backs off 600s instead of becoming the guard's second\n    witness) and the fourth, after the backoff's wait elapses and the task\n    is re-offered, is `consecutiveCount: 3` (backs off again, 1200s). The\n    old guard's own counter is left at 1 forever, never 3, so\n    `STAGNATION_MESSAGE` never appears -- requirement A.3's \"neither\n    increments nor resets\" holds for every re-poll from the second one\n    onward, not just the one named in its own worked example. task 014's\n    own sweep crashed an xdist worker on this exact node before this cure\n    (the module's own `_worker_sup` built `sup` directly rather than\n    through `tests.conftest.make_supervisor`, leaving the backoff's real\n    `asyncio.sleep(600)` unpatched -- `_patch_sleep_for_this_test()` now\n    closes that).","descriptionHtml":"<p>Four consecutive <code>external</code>-only claims on one task, no other<br />\nwitness: the first is honoured at face value (corroborated); the<br />\nsecond is requirement A.5's letter 3 own case (&quot;two consecutive<br />\nexternal-only claims&quot; -- the second does not get the grace the first<br />\ndid, so it is an ordinary stagnation witness, old counter -&gt; 1).</p>\n<pre><code>PRD v0.29 #279 cure (task 014's sweep): the THIRD and FOURTH no longer\nreach the old three-strike guard at all -- the second and third\nconsecutive uncorroborated claims are ALSO the first two of #279's own\nre-poll streak, so the third claim is #279's own `consecutiveCount: 2`\ntrigger (backs off 600s instead of becoming the guard's second\nwitness) and the fourth, after the backoff's wait elapses and the task\nis re-offered, is `consecutiveCount: 3` (backs off again, 1200s). The\nold guard's own counter is left at 1 forever, never 3, so\n`STAGNATION_MESSAGE` never appears -- requirement A.3's &quot;neither\nincrements nor resets&quot; holds for every re-poll from the second one\nonward, not just the one named in its own worked example. task 014's\nown sweep crashed an xdist worker on this exact node before this cure\n(the module's own `_worker_sup` built `sup` directly rather than\nthrough `tests.conftest.make_supervisor`, leaving the backoff's real\n`asyncio.sleep(600)` unpatched -- `_patch_sleep_for_this_test()` now\ncloses that).\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791941650430,"stop":1791941650430,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791941650431,"stop":1791941650431,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0